   "notes": "The paper proposes an activation function (GoLU), not a new network; it swaps GoLU into many existing architectures (ResNets, ViTs, GPT-2, Transformer-Big, DDPM, etc.). I described the language-model instantiation (nanoGPT GPT-2 series: babyGPT and GPT2-S) because it is the paper's transformer setting with stated sizes. GPT2-S d_ff is not stated. head_dim and kv_heads are not stated (not derived). GPT-2 internals (norm type and placement, positional embeddings, biases, tying, causal masking, residual adds) are not restated, so they are left not_stated. Only family is marked inherited, from the 'GPT-2 series' wording. Because the norms and residual adds are unstated, the block_ops are intentionally incomplete: they show only the attention sublayer and the GoLU FFN, with no explicit norm or residual-add nodes. The block is therefore not buildable as listed. The vocab/context sentence names 'babyGPT and nanoGPT'; I took 'nanoGPT' to mean GPT2-S."
